  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "By the numbers, dwarves are one of the best races in the Player’s Handbook.\n\tTheir ability score increases are good, and their other racial traits make\n\tthem durable and flexible enough to succeed in several classes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you’re using the Customizing Your Origins optional rules, the Dwarf is an\n\texcellent template for any class. Hill Dwarf is excellent for any build that\n\tneeds a few extra hit points, and Mountain Dwarf offers two +2 increases\n\t(unmatched by any other published race) and medium armor proficiency, which\n\tlargely solves the issue of AC for poorly-armored classes like the Wizard. For\n\tplayers looking for a solid mechanical basis for a build that doesn’t really\n\tcare about race, or for newer players looking to live a long, successful life,\n\tthe Dwarf is a great choice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you’re playing Baldur’s Gate 3, you might also enjoy our "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Baldur’s Gate 3 Dwarf Handbook",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/video-games/baldurs-gate-3/races/dwarf/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
